+### pi.invokeExtensionCommand(name, args?) (Familiar downstream)
+
+```typescript
+const command = pi.getCommands().find(c => c.source === "extension" && c.name === "review:2");
+if (command) await pi.invokeExtensionCommand(command.name, "unchanged args");
+```
+
+Invokes only an exact registered extension command (including collision suffixes),
+with a fresh command context. No leading slash, built-ins, skills, templates,
+input event, or model turn. Args default to `""` and are passed unchanged.
+The promise resolves after completion; unknown names, stale/uninitialized runtimes,
+busy sessions, and any nested or concurrent command reject. Handler Errors retain
+identity; other thrown values become `Error(String(value))`. Await/catch errors;
+programmatic invocation does not also emit an extension error event.
+
+The owning AgentSession's bound `isIdle()` must report true at admission. Active
+run tools/events cannot cross into command-only session controls: waiting there
+can deadlock on the caller itself (upstream commit `0d9fddec`, issue #2023).
+One runner-local command slot excludes even A -> B: different commands still
+mutate the same session. Calls reject rather than queue. The slot is released
+in `finally`, including handler failures and successful runtime replacement.
+Old captured pi/ctx remain stale after replacement or reload.
+
+This API is for an idle external human frontend, not deferred scheduling or a
+session-wide lock. Hosts must still gate other session actions during the handler.
+`AgentSession.prompt()` retains immediate command dispatch while streaming through
+an internal path, with the same exclusive guard and upstream report-and-consume
+error handling. The public API has no bypass option.
+
+Do not use a follow-up user message as a command queue: in 0.84.1 it is literal
+model-visible text. 0.84.2 adds `expandPromptTemplates` opt-in to `sendUserMessage`,
+but that is void, parses text, expands skills/templates, and dispatches commands
+before streaming queueing. It does not replace this awaited idle-only API.
+
 ### pi.getCommands()
 
 Get the slash commands available for invocation via `prompt` in the current session. Includes extension commands, prompt templates, and skill commands.
